WEBVTT

00:10:22.448 --> 00:10:24.659
I think he wants us to
pick up what he left off.

00:10:25.491 --> 00:10:27.457
Saving people, hunting things...

00:10:27.458 --> 00:10:28.585
Family business.

00:10:29.664 --> 00:10:32.635
I don't understand the blind
faith you have in the man.

00:10:32.636 --> 00:10:34.146
It's called being a good son!

00:10:36.604 --> 00:10:39.693
You were just pissed off you
couldn't control me anymore!

00:10:47.688 --> 00:10:49.162
If only your boys

00:10:49.810 --> 00:10:51.694
Knew how much their daddy loved them.

00:11:00.202 --> 00:11:01.060
Dad?

00:11:06.918 --> 00:11:09.155
Did he say anything to you? No.

00:11:11.689 --> 00:11:13.513
I'm dealing with dad's death.

00:11:14.698 --> 00:11:15.665
Are you?

00:13:08.280 --> 00:13:09.654
Listen to her purr.

00:13:09.658 --> 00:13:11.325
You ever heard anything so sweet?

00:13:11.327 --> 00:13:14.134
If you two want to get a
room, just let me know, Dean.

00:13:14.139 --> 00:13:15.855
Oh, don't listen to him, baby.

00:13:15.860 --> 00:13:17.123
He doesn't understand.

00:13:18.427 --> 00:13:19.855
You're in a good mood.

00:13:19.860 --> 00:13:21.044
Why shouldn't I be?

00:13:21.920 --> 00:13:22.882
No reason.

00:13:22.897 --> 00:13:24.105
I got my car,

00:13:24.230 --> 00:13:25.364
I got a case.

00:13:25.628 --> 00:13:26.663
Things are looking up.

00:13:28.479 --> 00:13:31.825
You hear of a couple of severed
heads and a pile of dead cows,

00:13:31.830 --> 00:13:33.534
And you're mr. Sunshine.

00:13:34.328 --> 00:13:35.763
How far to Red Lodge?

00:13:36.380 --> 00:13:38.515
Uh, about another 300 miles.

00:13:39.297 --> 00:13:40.185
Good.

00:13:45.129 --> 00:13:47.482
The murder investigation is ongoing,

00:13:47.499 --> 00:13:49.694
And that's all I can share
with the press at this time.

00:13:49.699 --> 00:13:51.583
Sure, sure, we understand
that. But just for the record,

00:13:51.708 --> 00:13:53.403
You found the first uh...

00:13:53.787 --> 00:13:55.135
Head last week, correct?

00:13:55.779 --> 00:13:57.665
Okay, and the other, a...

00:13:57.668 --> 00:14:00.124
Christina Flannigan?
That was two days ago.

00:14:00.127 --> 00:14:01.395
Excuse me, Sir.

00:14:02.468 --> 00:14:03.504
Thank you.

00:14:03.978 --> 00:14:05.664
Sorry, boys, time's up.

00:14:05.669 --> 00:14:06.922
We're done here. One last question.

00:14:06.929 --> 00:14:08.422
What about the cattle? Excuse me?

00:14:08.427 --> 00:14:09.795
You know, the cows found dead,

00:14:09.927 --> 00:14:13.195
Split open, drained...
Over a dozen cases.

00:14:14.210 --> 00:14:15.074
What about them?

00:14:15.079 --> 00:14:16.725
So, you don't think
there's a connection?

00:14:18.078 --> 00:14:21.274
Connection with... First,

00:14:21.288 --> 00:14:23.604
Cattle mutilations, now...

00:14:23.610 --> 00:14:26.535
Now, two murders? Kind of
sounds like ritual stuff.

00:14:26.537 --> 00:14:29.235
You know, like satanic
cult ritual stuff.

00:14:38.379 --> 00:14:40.343
You're not kidding. No.

00:14:42.997 --> 00:14:45.562
Those cows aren't being mutilated.

00:14:45.940 --> 00:14:47.985
You want to know how I know? How?

00:14:48.297 --> 00:14:51.293
Because there's no such
thing as cattle mutilation.

00:14:51.300 --> 00:14:53.545
Cow drops, leave it in the sun,

00:14:53.549 --> 00:14:57.275
Within 48 hours the bloat
will split it open so clean

00:14:57.278 --> 00:14:58.953
It's just about surgical.

00:14:58.959 --> 00:15:03.015
The bodily fluids fall down
into the ground, get soaked up,

00:15:03.019 --> 00:15:05.322
'Cause that's what gravity does.

00:15:05.639 --> 00:15:08.523
But, hey, it could be Satan.

00:15:08.678 --> 00:15:11.645
What newspaper did
you say you worked for?

00:15:13.657 --> 00:15:16.024
World Weekly News. Weekly World News.

00:15:16.027 --> 00:15:18.864
World... I'm new. Weekly world.

00:15:20.758 --> 00:15:23.215
Get out of my office.

00:15:32.178 --> 00:15:33.135
John.

00:15:33.138 --> 00:15:35.145
Jeff. Jeff, I know that.

00:15:35.690 --> 00:15:37.965
Dr. Dorkin needs to see you
in his office right away.

00:15:37.968 --> 00:15:39.752
But dr. Dorkin's on vacation.

00:15:39.757 --> 00:15:42.322
He's back, and he's pissed,
and he's screaming for you, man.

00:15:42.327 --> 00:15:43.815
So, if i were you, I would...

00:15:49.457 --> 00:15:51.815
Hey, those satanists in Florida, they
marked their victims, didn't they?

00:15:51.829 --> 00:15:53.775
Yeah, reverse pentacle on the forehead.

00:15:54.959 --> 00:15:58.055
So much of that crap happens in Florida.

00:16:04.118 --> 00:16:05.573
All right. Open it.

00:16:06.357 --> 00:16:07.265
You open it.

00:16:08.738 --> 00:16:09.675
Wuss.

00:16:19.018 --> 00:16:20.395
Well, no pentagram.

00:16:21.160 --> 00:16:23.164
Poor girl. Maybe we should, uh,

00:16:23.169 --> 00:16:24.585
Look in her mouth, see if

00:16:24.940 --> 00:16:28.083
This wacko stuffed anything down her
throat, you know, kind of like the moth in

00:16:28.379 --> 00:16:29.643
"Silence of the Lambs".

00:16:30.287 --> 00:16:32.694
Yeah, yeah, go ahead. No, you go ahead.

00:16:33.259 --> 00:16:34.285
W hat?

00:16:34.288 --> 00:16:35.772
"Put the lotion in the basket".

00:16:36.650 --> 00:16:38.652
Right, yeah, I'm the wuss, huh?

00:16:39.528 --> 00:16:40.465
Whatever.

00:16:47.337 --> 00:16:48.655
Dean, get me a bucket.

00:16:48.677 --> 00:16:50.515
Find something? No, I'm gonna puke.

00:16:54.659 --> 00:16:56.612
All right, lift her lip up again. What?

00:16:57.910 --> 00:17:00.564
You want me to throw up, is that
it? No, I think I saw something.

00:17:05.310 --> 00:17:06.704
Is that a hole?

00:17:08.638 --> 00:17:10.855
It's a tooth. Sam, that's a fang.

00:17:13.709 --> 00:17:16.615
Retractable set of vampire
fangs. You got to be kidding me.

00:17:16.620 --> 00:17:18.492
Well, this changes things.

00:17:18.727 --> 00:17:19.765
You think?

00:17:46.927 --> 00:17:48.313
How's it going?

00:17:48.709 --> 00:17:49.812
Living  the dream.

00:17:49.817 --> 00:17:51.553
What can I get for
you? Two beers, please.

00:17:53.769 --> 00:17:55.343
So, we're looking for some people.

00:17:56.468 --> 00:17:58.142
Sure. It's hard to be lonely.

00:18:00.748 --> 00:18:02.052
Yeah, but, um,

00:18:03.597 --> 00:18:04.763
That's not what I meant.

00:18:11.898 --> 00:18:13.752
Great. So, these people

00:18:13.830 --> 00:18:15.532
Would've moved here
about six months ago,

00:18:15.537 --> 00:18:17.384
Probably pretty rowdy, like to drink.

00:18:17.390 --> 00:18:19.054
Yeah, real night owls, you know?

00:18:19.057 --> 00:18:20.972
Sleep all day, party all night.

00:18:21.099 --> 00:18:23.335
Barker farm got leased
out a couple months ago.

00:18:23.399 --> 00:18:25.593
Real winners. They've
been in here a lot.

00:18:25.689 --> 00:18:27.752
Drinkers, noisy.

00:18:28.429 --> 00:18:30.152
I had to 86 them once or twice.

00:18:33.687 --> 00:18:34.472
Thanks.

00:19:49.688 --> 00:19:51.242
Smile. What?

00:19:51.247 --> 00:19:53.614
Show us those pearly
whites. For the love of...

00:19:53.950 --> 00:19:55.802
You want to stick that
thing some place else?

00:19:55.818 --> 00:19:56.975
I'm not a vampire.

00:19:58.190 --> 00:19:58.894
Yeah, that's right.

00:19:59.117 --> 00:20:00.305
I heard you guys in there.

00:20:00.309 --> 00:20:02.273
What do you know about
vampires? How to kill them.

00:20:02.467 --> 00:20:03.653
Now, seriously, bro,

00:20:03.856 --> 00:20:05.593
That knife's making me itch.

00:20:09.597 --> 00:20:10.742
Easy there, chachi.

00:20:18.459 --> 00:20:19.205
See?

00:20:20.378 --> 00:20:21.224
Fangless.

00:20:21.550 --> 00:20:22.644
Happy?

00:20:25.677 --> 00:20:26.402
Now,

00:20:27.318 --> 00:20:28.373
Who the hell are you?

00:20:29.297 --> 00:20:31.134
Sam and Dean Winchester.

00:20:34.033 --> 00:20:35.044
I can't believe it.

00:20:35.612 --> 00:20:37.014
You know, I met your old man once.

00:20:37.012 --> 00:20:38.430
Hell of a guy, great hunter.

00:20:39.769 --> 00:20:40.795
I heard he passed.

00:20:41.317 --> 00:20:42.543
I'm sorry.

00:20:42.827 --> 00:20:44.021
It's big shoes,

00:20:44.170 --> 00:20:46.102
But, from what I hear,
you guys fill them.

00:20:46.220 --> 00:20:48.102
Great trackers, good in a tight spot.

00:20:48.150 --> 00:20:49.845
You seem to know a lot about our family.

00:20:49.849 --> 00:20:51.083
Word travels fast.

00:20:51.178 --> 00:20:53.543
You know how hunters
talk. No, we don't actully.

00:20:53.690 --> 00:20:55.692
I guess there's a lot your
dad never told you, huh?

00:20:58.068 --> 00:20:59.302
So, um...

00:21:00.998 --> 00:21:02.802
So, those two vampires,
they were yours, huh?

00:21:02.809 --> 00:21:03.733
Yep.

00:21:03.817 --> 00:21:04.773
Been here two weeks.

00:21:04.778 --> 00:21:06.713
Did you check out that
Barker farm? It's a bust.

00:21:06.718 --> 00:21:08.233
Just a bunch of hippie freaks.

00:21:08.388 --> 00:21:10.552
Though they could kill with
that patchouli smell alone.

00:21:10.557 --> 00:21:11.572
Where's the nest, then?

00:21:14.067 --> 00:21:15.213
I got this one covered.

00:21:16.298 --> 00:21:17.375
Look, don't get me wrong.

00:21:17.379 --> 00:21:18.963
It's a real pleasure meeting you fellas,

00:21:19.028 --> 00:21:20.792
But I've been on this
thing for over a year.

00:21:21.467 --> 00:21:24.461
I killed a fang back in Austin,
tracked the nest all the way up here.

00:21:24.929 --> 00:21:25.753
I'll finish it.

00:21:26.677 --> 00:21:27.985
We could help.

00:21:28.028 --> 00:21:29.164
Thanks, but, uh,

00:21:29.490 --> 00:21:31.182
I'm kind of a
go-It-Alone type of guy.

00:21:31.239 --> 00:21:33.021
But man, I've been itching for a hunt.

00:21:33.477 --> 00:21:34.255
Sorry.

00:21:34.259 --> 00:21:36.942
But, hey, I hear there's a
chupacabra two states over.

00:21:37.119 --> 00:21:38.572
Go ahead and knock yourselves out.

00:21:44.880 --> 00:21:46.472
It was real good meeting you, though.

00:21:47.519 --> 00:21:49.285
I'll buy you a drink on the flip side.

00:24:29.128 --> 00:24:30.172
So, uh,

00:24:30.490 --> 00:24:32.375
I guess I got to buy you that drink.

00:24:51.259 --> 00:24:52.034
No, no,

00:24:52.249 --> 00:24:53.094
I got it.

00:24:53.099 --> 00:24:54.503
Come on. I insist.

00:24:55.599 --> 00:24:56.492
Thank you, sweetie.

00:25:00.059 --> 00:25:01.484
Another one bites the dust.

00:25:01.489 --> 00:25:02.215
That's right.

00:25:12.557 --> 00:25:15.513
You gave that big-Ass fang one
hell of a haircut, my friend.

00:25:15.527 --> 00:25:17.094
That was you. That was beautiful,

00:25:17.108 --> 00:25:19.403
Absolutely beautiful. Yep.

00:25:20.350 --> 00:25:22.114
You all right, Sammy? Yeah, fine.

00:25:22.117 --> 00:25:23.414
Lighten up a little, Sammy.

00:25:23.626 --> 00:25:25.403
He's the only one who
gets to call me that.

00:25:25.769 --> 00:25:26.593
Okay.

00:25:26.830 --> 00:25:27.822
No offense meant.

00:25:27.827 --> 00:25:29.864
Just celebrating a
little. Job well done.

00:25:29.870 --> 00:25:31.305
Right. Well, um,

00:25:32.000 --> 00:25:35.304
Decapitations aren't my
idea of a good time, I guess.

00:25:35.307 --> 00:25:37.804
Oh,  come on, man, it's
not like it was human.

00:25:37.807 --> 00:25:39.892
You got to have a little
more fun in that job.

00:25:39.898 --> 00:25:41.762
See, that's what I've
been trying to tell him.

00:25:41.778 --> 00:25:43.572
You could learn a thing
or two from this guy.

00:25:48.097 --> 00:25:49.244
Yeah,  I bet I could.

00:25:49.597 --> 00:25:50.362
Look,

00:25:50.458 --> 00:25:52.055
I'm not gonna bring you guys down.

00:25:52.057 --> 00:25:53.585
I'm just gonna go back to the motel.

00:25:53.789 --> 00:25:55.025
You sure? Yeah.

00:25:58.396 --> 00:25:59.275
Sammy...

00:26:01.649 --> 00:26:04.173
Remind me to beat that buzzkill
out of you later, all right?

00:26:08.248 --> 00:26:09.722
Something I said? No, no.

00:26:09.727 --> 00:26:11.245
He just gets that way sometimes.

00:26:12.539 --> 00:26:13.572
Tell you what,

00:26:14.359 --> 00:26:16.012
Match quarters for the next round.

00:26:34.018 --> 00:26:34.771
So

00:26:35.247 --> 00:26:36.452
I picked up this crossbow,

00:26:36.896 --> 00:26:38.434
And I hit that ugly sucker.

00:26:38.530 --> 00:26:39.894
The silver-Tipped arrow,

00:26:40.120 --> 00:26:41.045
Right in his heart.

00:26:41.748 --> 00:26:43.505
Sammy's waiting in the car, and

00:26:43.510 --> 00:26:45.704
Me and my dad take the
thing into the woods,

00:26:46.360 --> 00:26:47.775
Burn it to a crisp.

00:26:48.189 --> 00:26:51.314
I'm sitting there, and I'm looking into
the fire, and I'm thinking to myself,

00:26:52.519 --> 00:26:54.055
I'm 16 years old

00:26:55.207 --> 00:26:57.653
Kids my age are worried about pimples,

00:26:57.657 --> 00:26:58.783
Prom dates.

00:26:59.609 --> 00:27:01.664
I'm seeing things that
they'll never even know,

00:27:02.509 --> 00:27:03.844
Never even dream of.

00:27:06.830 --> 00:27:08.284
So right then, I just sort of...

00:27:08.537 --> 00:27:09.863
Embraced the life?

00:27:11.417 --> 00:27:12.232
Yeah.

00:27:12.468 --> 00:27:13.435
Yeah.

00:27:15.177 --> 00:27:15.963
Yeah.

00:27:17.628 --> 00:27:18.764
How'd you get started?

00:27:18.770 --> 00:27:21.662
First time I saw a
vampire, I was barely 18.

00:27:21.830 --> 00:27:23.474
Home alone with my sister.

00:27:23.479 --> 00:27:26.563
I hear the window break in her room.

00:27:27.637 --> 00:27:29.542
I grabbed my dad's gun, run in,

00:27:29.549 --> 00:27:31.023
Try to get it off her.

00:27:31.028 --> 00:27:32.152
It was too late.

00:27:32.548 --> 00:27:34.092
So I shoot the damn thing,

00:27:34.398 --> 00:27:37.903
Which, of course, is about as useful
as snapping it with a rubber band.

00:27:38.157 --> 00:27:39.503
It rushes me,

00:27:39.507 --> 00:27:43.414
Picks me up, flings me across
the room, knocks me out cold.

00:27:43.419 --> 00:27:45.113
When I wake up,

00:27:45.490 --> 00:27:47.373
The vampire's gone...

00:27:47.687 --> 00:27:49.732
My sister's gone.

00:27:49.909 --> 00:27:51.243
And then?

00:27:51.377 --> 00:27:52.682
Then...

00:27:55.140 --> 00:27:57.053
Try explaining that one to your family.

00:27:58.877 --> 00:27:59.993
So I left home...

00:28:01.618 --> 00:28:04.144
And then bummed around
looking for information.

00:28:04.819 --> 00:28:06.725
How you track them, how you kill them.

00:28:08.638 --> 00:28:10.344
And I found that fang.

00:28:11.328 --> 00:28:13.115
It was my first kill.

00:28:15.097 --> 00:28:16.543
Sorry about your sister.

00:28:17.148 --> 00:28:17.984
Yeah.

00:28:19.627 --> 00:28:20.632
She was beautiful.

00:28:21.387 --> 00:28:23.054
I can still see her, you know,

00:28:23.349 --> 00:28:24.602
The way she was.

00:28:30.378 --> 00:28:32.384
But, hey, that was a long time ago.

00:28:33.180 --> 00:28:34.113
I mean,

00:28:34.120 --> 00:28:34.975
Your dad...

00:28:36.018 --> 00:28:37.053
It's got to be rough.

00:28:37.528 --> 00:28:38.424
Yeah.

00:28:40.267 --> 00:28:41.523
Yeah, you know,

00:28:41.809 --> 00:28:43.305
He was just one of those guys.

00:28:44.589 --> 00:28:46.072
Took some terrible beatings,

00:28:46.757 --> 00:28:48.012
Just kept coming.

00:28:49.009 --> 00:28:50.423
So you're always saying to yourself,

00:28:51.637 --> 00:28:52.513
He's indestructible.

00:28:53.737 --> 00:28:56.143
He'll always be around.
Nothing can kill my dad.

00:28:58.059 --> 00:28:59.163
And just like that...

00:29:01.519 --> 00:29:02.442
He's gone.

00:29:10.218 --> 00:29:12.195
I can't talk about this to Sammy.

00:29:12.668 --> 00:29:14.824
No, I got to keep my game face on.

00:29:16.168 --> 00:29:17.592
But, uh...

00:29:18.677 --> 00:29:21.393
Truth is, I'm not handling it very well.

00:29:24.578 --> 00:29:26.243
I feel like I have this...

00:29:26.249 --> 00:29:27.653
Hole inside you?

00:29:28.769 --> 00:29:31.772
And it just gets bigger and
bigger and darker and darker?

00:29:34.619 --> 00:29:35.505
Good.

00:29:36.118 --> 00:29:37.174
You can use it.

00:29:37.338 --> 00:29:38.523
Keeps you hungry.

00:29:39.359 --> 00:29:40.295
Trust me,

00:29:40.300 --> 00:29:42.872
There's plenty out there needs
killing, and this will help you do it.

00:29:45.057 --> 00:29:46.855
It's not a crime to need your job.

00:29:55.569 --> 00:29:56.623
Hardrails roadhouse.

00:29:56.679 --> 00:29:58.585
Hey, Ellen. Sam Winchester.

00:29:58.590 --> 00:30:00.774
Sam, it's good to hear from you.

00:30:01.107 --> 00:30:04.215
You boys are okay, aren't you?
Yeah, yeah, everything's fine.

00:30:04.369 --> 00:30:05.565
Got a question.

00:30:05.569 --> 00:30:06.382
Yeah, shoot.

00:30:06.389 --> 00:30:08.672
You  ever run across a
guy named Gordon Walker?

00:30:08.947 --> 00:30:10.103
I know Gordon.

00:30:10.107 --> 00:30:11.795
And? He's a real good hunter.

00:30:11.799 --> 00:30:14.475
Why you're asking, sweetie?
We ran into him on a job.

00:30:14.610 --> 00:30:17.423
We're kind of working with
him. Don't do that, Sam.

00:30:18.568 --> 00:30:19.362
I...

00:30:19.598 --> 00:30:21.333
I thought you said he was a good hunter.

00:30:21.429 --> 00:30:23.645
Yeah, and Hannibal Lecter's
a good psychiatrist.

00:30:23.660 --> 00:30:26.584
He is dangerous to everyone
and everything around him.

00:30:26.759 --> 00:30:29.562
If he's working on a job, you boys
just let him handle it and you move on.

00:30:29.639 --> 00:30:30.872
Ellen... No, Sam,

00:30:30.877 --> 00:30:33.045
You just listen to what
I'm telling you, okay?

00:30:35.268 --> 00:30:36.395
Right, okay.

00:30:36.950 --> 00:30:38.483
You know why I love this life?

00:30:39.858 --> 00:30:41.652
It's all black and white.

00:30:41.949 --> 00:30:43.192
There's no maybe.

00:30:43.518 --> 00:30:44.935
You  find the bad thing,

00:30:44.939 --> 00:30:45.663
Kill it.

00:30:46.268 --> 00:30:49.055
Most people spend their
lives in shades of gray.

00:30:49.957 --> 00:30:52.034
Is this right? Is that wrong?

00:30:52.400 --> 00:30:53.403
Not us.

00:30:53.960 --> 00:30:56.182
Not sure Sammy would
agree with you, but, uh...

00:30:56.410 --> 00:30:58.634
Doesn't seem like your
brother's much like us.

00:30:59.938 --> 00:31:01.354
I'm not saying he's wrong.

00:31:01.668 --> 00:31:02.675
Just different.

00:31:02.917 --> 00:31:03.944
You and me,

00:31:04.028 --> 00:31:05.405
We were born to do this.

00:31:05.899 --> 00:31:07.144
It's in our blood.

00:33:03.417 --> 00:33:04.292
Wait!

00:33:05.259 --> 00:33:06.653
Step back, Eli.

00:33:14.329 --> 00:33:16.542
My name's Lenore. I'm
not gonna hurt you.

00:33:16.550 --> 00:33:18.244
We just need to talk. Talk?

00:33:18.500 --> 00:33:19.475
Yeah, okay. But

00:33:19.477 --> 00:33:22.665
I might have a tough time paying
attention to much besides Eli's teeth.

00:33:22.680 --> 00:33:26.492
He won't hurt you, either. You have my
word. Your word? Oh, yeah, great, thanks.

00:33:26.497 --> 00:33:29.242
Listen, lady, no offense, but you're
not the first vampire I've met.

00:33:29.248 --> 00:33:30.764
We're not like the others.

00:33:30.778 --> 00:33:32.182
We don't kill humans,

00:33:32.189 --> 00:33:34.422
And we don't drink their blood.
We haven't for a long time.

00:33:34.470 --> 00:33:36.883
What is this? Some kinda joke?
Notice you're still alive.

00:33:41.320 --> 00:33:45.185
Okay, uh, correct me if I'm wrong here,
but shouldn't you be starving to death?

00:33:45.197 --> 00:33:46.733
We found other ways.

00:33:46.737 --> 00:33:47.633
Cattle blood.

00:33:48.008 --> 00:33:49.752
You're telling me you're
responsible for all the...

00:33:49.759 --> 00:33:52.153
It's not ideal. In
fact, it's disgusting.

00:33:52.487 --> 00:33:55.942
But it allows us to
get by. Okay. Uh, why?

00:33:55.960 --> 00:33:56.984
Survival.

00:33:57.749 --> 00:33:59.992
No deaths, no missing locals, no

00:33:59.999 --> 00:34:03.092
Reason for people like you to
come looking for people like us.

00:34:03.937 --> 00:34:05.435
And we blend in.

00:34:06.050 --> 00:34:08.145
Our kind is practically extinct.

00:34:08.427 --> 00:34:11.534
It turns out we weren't as high
up the food chain as we imagined.

00:34:11.538 --> 00:34:13.655
Why are we explaining
ourselves to this killer?

00:34:13.659 --> 00:34:15.153
Eli. We choke

00:34:15.157 --> 00:34:17.704
On cow's blood so that
none of them suffer.

00:34:17.710 --> 00:34:20.192
Tonight, they murdered
Conrad, and they celebrated.

00:34:20.199 --> 00:34:23.163
Eli, that's enough.
Yeah, Eli, that's enough.

00:34:23.168 --> 00:34:25.172
What's done is done.

00:34:25.747 --> 00:34:28.681
We're leaving this town tonight.
Then, why did you bring me here?

00:34:28.689 --> 00:34:30.521
Why are you even talking to me?

00:34:30.530 --> 00:34:32.114
Believe me, I'd rather not.

00:34:32.117 --> 00:34:33.474
But I know your kind.

00:34:33.480 --> 00:34:35.283
Once you have the scent,
you'll keep tracking us.

00:34:35.288 --> 00:34:36.693
It doesn't matter where we go.

00:34:37.260 --> 00:34:38.753
Hunters will find us.

00:34:38.898 --> 00:34:40.625
So you're asking us not to follow you.

00:34:40.628 --> 00:34:42.882
We have a right to live.
We're not hurting anyone.

00:34:42.889 --> 00:34:44.132
Right, so you keep saying.

00:34:44.188 --> 00:34:46.563
But give me one good reason
why I should believe you.

00:34:49.640 --> 00:34:50.762
Fine.

00:34:52.498 --> 00:34:54.181
You know what I'm going to do?

00:34:57.086 --> 00:34:59.342
I'm going to let you go.

00:35:02.278 --> 00:35:03.793
Take him back.

00:35:03.810 --> 00:35:05.194
Not a mark on him.

00:35:34.720 --> 00:35:37.195
This is the best
pattern I can establish.

00:35:37.489 --> 00:35:39.015
It's sketchy, at best.

00:35:39.016 --> 00:35:41.372
Looks like it's all coming
from this side of town,

00:35:41.479 --> 00:35:43.414
Which means the nest would be
around here someplace, right?

00:35:43.417 --> 00:35:44.945
Yep, that's what I'm thinking.

00:35:45.248 --> 00:35:48.653
Problem is, there's
35, 40 farms out there.

00:35:48.860 --> 00:35:50.923
I searched about half
of them already but

00:35:50.927 --> 00:35:52.222
Nothing yet.

00:35:52.367 --> 00:35:53.912
They're covering their tracks real good.

00:35:53.918 --> 00:35:55.954
I guess we'll just have
to search the other half.

00:35:58.967 --> 00:36:00.565
What time is it? Where is Sam?

00:36:01.289 --> 00:36:02.885
Car's parked outside.

00:36:03.210 --> 00:36:04.963
Probably went for a walk.

00:36:05.358 --> 00:36:08.382
Seems like the take-A-Walk
type. Yeah, he is, but...

00:36:12.420 --> 00:36:13.382
Where you been?

00:36:13.699 --> 00:36:15.204
Can I talk to you alone?

00:36:16.438 --> 00:36:17.935
You mind chilling out
for a couple of minutes?

00:36:24.077 --> 00:36:25.953
Dean, maybe we got to rethink this hunt.

00:36:25.958 --> 00:36:27.063
What are you talking about?

00:36:27.069 --> 00:36:28.052
Where were you?

00:36:29.710 --> 00:36:30.802
In the nest.

00:36:30.969 --> 00:36:31.965
You found it?

00:36:32.048 --> 00:36:33.614
They found me, man.

00:36:34.257 --> 00:36:35.984
How did you get out?
How many did you kill?

00:36:37.228 --> 00:36:38.144
None.

00:36:38.560 --> 00:36:41.554
Sam, they didn't just let you
go. That's exactly what they did.

00:36:41.640 --> 00:36:43.021
All right, well, where is it?

00:36:43.627 --> 00:36:45.074
I was blindfolded. I don't know.

00:36:45.289 --> 00:36:46.315
You got to know something.

00:36:46.318 --> 00:36:47.685
We went over that
bridge outside of town,

00:36:47.690 --> 00:36:49.663
But Dean, listen, maybe
we shouldn't go after them.

00:36:49.668 --> 00:36:51.632
Why not? I don't think
they're like other vampires.

00:36:51.720 --> 00:36:53.015
I don't think they're killing people.

00:36:53.016 --> 00:36:53.882
You're joking.

00:36:55.577 --> 00:36:57.014
Then, how do they stay alive

00:36:57.019 --> 00:36:58.675
Or undead or whatever the hell they are?

00:36:58.688 --> 00:37:00.063
The cattle mutilations.

00:37:00.140 --> 00:37:01.972
They said they live off of animal blood.

00:37:02.037 --> 00:37:03.092
And you believed them?

00:37:03.288 --> 00:37:04.283
Look at me, Dean.

00:37:05.618 --> 00:37:07.283
They let me go without a scratch.

00:37:07.838 --> 00:37:08.942
Wait, so you're saying...

00:37:10.578 --> 00:37:12.195
No, man. No way.

00:37:12.257 --> 00:37:14.302
I don't know why they let
you go. I don't really care.

00:37:14.780 --> 00:37:15.832
We find them, and we waste them.

00:37:16.578 --> 00:37:17.614
Why?

00:37:19.349 --> 00:37:21.652
What part of vampires
don't you understand, Sam?

00:37:21.659 --> 00:37:24.012
If it's supernatural, we kill
it. End of story. That's our job.

00:37:24.016 --> 00:37:27.023
No, Dean, that is not our
job. Our job is hunting evil.

00:37:27.180 --> 00:37:29.555
And if these things aren't
killing people, they're not evil.

00:37:29.569 --> 00:37:31.284
Of course, they're killing
people. That's what they do.

00:37:31.288 --> 00:37:32.742
They're all the same, Sam.

00:37:32.787 --> 00:37:34.262
They're not human, okay?

00:37:34.268 --> 00:37:35.824
We have to exterminate
every last one of them.

00:37:35.829 --> 00:37:38.632
No, Dean, I don't think so,
all right? Not this time.

00:37:38.637 --> 00:37:41.033
Gordon's been on those
vamps for a year. He knows.

00:37:41.039 --> 00:37:43.324
Gordon? You're taking his word for it?

00:37:43.329 --> 00:37:45.445
That's right. Ellen says he's bad news.

00:37:45.609 --> 00:37:46.943
You called Ellen?

00:37:47.430 --> 00:37:49.713
And I'm supposed to listen to
her? We barely know her, Sam.

00:37:49.717 --> 00:37:51.292
No thanks. I'll go with Gordon.

00:37:51.297 --> 00:37:53.784
Right, 'cause Gordon's
such an old friend.

00:37:54.757 --> 00:37:56.164
You don't think I can see what this is?

00:37:56.168 --> 00:37:58.065
What are you talking about?
He's a substitute for dad.

00:37:58.277 --> 00:38:00.025
A poor one. Shut up, Sam.

00:38:00.028 --> 00:38:02.744
He's not even close,
Dean, not on his best day.

00:38:02.750 --> 00:38:05.074
You know what, I'm not even...
You slap on this fake smile,

00:38:05.077 --> 00:38:08.144
But I can see right through it
'cause I know how you feel, Dean.

00:38:08.149 --> 00:38:09.141
Dad's dead.

00:38:09.157 --> 00:38:11.963
And he left a hole, and it
hurts so bad you can't take it.

00:38:11.970 --> 00:38:14.534
But you can't just fill up that
hole with whoever you want to.

00:38:15.277 --> 00:38:16.993
It's an insult to his memory.

00:38:19.238 --> 00:38:19.993
Okay.

00:38:31.628 --> 00:38:32.913
You can hit me all you want.

00:38:33.050 --> 00:38:34.073
It won't change anything.

00:38:34.569 --> 00:38:35.793
I'm going to that nest.

00:38:35.899 --> 00:38:37.342
You don't want to tell me where it is?

00:38:37.349 --> 00:38:38.135
Fine.

00:38:38.448 --> 00:38:39.565
I'll find it myself.

00:38:43.847 --> 00:38:44.583
Dean.

00:38:48.697 --> 00:38:49.485
Gordon?

00:38:52.387 --> 00:38:53.632
You think he went after them?

00:38:53.748 --> 00:38:54.474
Probably.

00:38:54.476 --> 00:38:56.173
Dean, we have to stop him. Really?

00:38:56.179 --> 00:38:57.792
'Cause I say we lend a hand.

00:38:57.800 --> 00:38:59.855
Just give me the benefit
of the doubt, would you?!

00:38:59.860 --> 00:39:00.972
You owe me that.

00:39:00.979 --> 00:39:02.045
Yeah, we'll see.

00:39:02.389 --> 00:39:03.695
I'll drive. Give me the keys.

00:39:07.487 --> 00:39:08.824
He snaked the keys.

00:39:09.569 --> 00:39:10.731
I can't believe this.

00:39:11.969 --> 00:39:13.534
I just fixed her up, too.

00:39:18.628 --> 00:39:20.774
So, the bridge, is that all you got?

00:39:20.818 --> 00:39:23.204
The bridge was 4 and 1/2
minutes from their farm.

00:39:23.268 --> 00:39:24.194
How do you know?

00:39:25.528 --> 00:39:26.385
I counted.

00:39:28.878 --> 00:39:32.503
Took a left out of the farm, then
turned right onto a dirt road,

00:39:32.998 --> 00:39:35.104
Followed that for two
minutes slightly uphill

00:39:35.108 --> 00:39:37.525
Then took another quick
right, and we hit the bridge.

00:39:37.836 --> 00:39:39.135
You're good.

00:39:40.257 --> 00:39:42.085
You're a monster pain in the ass...

00:39:43.317 --> 00:39:44.465
But you're good.

00:39:57.769 --> 00:40:00.375
In the truck, thank you.
We can't leave like this.

00:40:00.550 --> 00:40:01.525
Lenore,

00:40:02.329 --> 00:40:04.244
Listen to me. We need to stay and fight.

00:40:04.248 --> 00:40:06.534
They were my friends,
too, Eli, my family.

00:40:06.537 --> 00:40:08.225
That's not what I'm talking about.

00:40:08.617 --> 00:40:10.802
This is self-Defense.
Kill or be killed.

00:40:10.806 --> 00:40:12.762
They can't hunt us if they're dead.

00:40:12.949 --> 00:40:15.472
Killing those three
wouldn't solve anything.

00:40:15.978 --> 00:40:18.954
There's more where they
came from. We're outnumbered.

00:40:19.368 --> 00:40:20.461
This...

00:40:20.619 --> 00:40:22.503
This is all we can do.

00:40:23.047 --> 00:40:25.713
Try and reason... You can't
reason with these people.

00:40:26.387 --> 00:40:28.235
They're gonna kill us all anyway.

00:40:29.447 --> 00:40:31.625
We should at least take
a few of them with us.

00:40:35.079 --> 00:40:36.702
I'm not giving up hope.

00:40:38.470 --> 00:40:39.913
If we can change,

00:40:40.708 --> 00:40:42.073
They can change.

00:40:42.219 --> 00:40:45.333
Now, go into town and gather the others.

00:40:45.336 --> 00:40:47.092
We leave before sunrise.

00:42:14.057 --> 00:42:15.663
Dead man's blood, bitch.

00:42:55.476 --> 00:42:58.884
Sam, Dean, come on in.
Gordon, what's going on?

00:42:58.887 --> 00:43:01.605
Just poisoning Lenore here
with some dead man's blood.

00:43:01.606 --> 00:43:04.125
She's gonna tell us where all her
little friends are, aren't you?

00:43:04.368 --> 00:43:05.145
Want to help?

00:43:05.208 --> 00:43:06.972
Look, man... Grab a knife.

00:43:07.730 --> 00:43:09.961
I was just about to
start in on the fingers.

00:43:17.069 --> 00:43:18.005
Let's all just

00:43:18.139 --> 00:43:19.273
Chill out, huh?

00:43:20.050 --> 00:43:22.702
I'm completely chill.
Gordon, put the knife down.

00:43:22.967 --> 00:43:24.994
It sounds like it's
Sam here needs to chill.

00:43:25.159 --> 00:43:27.202
Just step away from her, all right?

00:43:32.737 --> 00:43:33.743
You're right.

00:43:35.407 --> 00:43:36.792
I'm wasting my time here.

00:43:37.617 --> 00:43:39.163
This bitch will never talk.

00:43:40.668 --> 00:43:42.704
Might as well put her out of her misery.

00:43:43.427 --> 00:43:45.934
I just sharpened it, so
it's completely humane.

00:43:46.478 --> 00:43:49.452
Gordon, I'm letting her go.
You're not doing a damn thing.

00:43:52.380 --> 00:43:54.993
Gordon, let's talk about this.
What's there to talk about?

00:43:54.998 --> 00:43:56.353
It's like I said, Dean.

00:43:56.358 --> 00:43:58.524
No shades of gray. Yeah,

00:43:58.528 --> 00:43:59.774
I hear you.

00:44:00.168 --> 00:44:02.203
And I know how you feel. Do you?

00:44:02.208 --> 00:44:05.453
The vampire that killed your
sister deserved to die, but this...

00:44:06.978 --> 00:44:08.363
Killed my sister.

00:44:09.119 --> 00:44:12.485
That filthy fang didn't kill
my sister. It turned her,

00:44:13.119 --> 00:44:14.523
Made her one of them.

00:44:15.068 --> 00:44:18.142
So I hunted her down
and I killed her myself.

00:44:19.500 --> 00:44:20.613
You did what?

00:44:20.617 --> 00:44:22.914
It wasn't my sister
anymore. It wasn't human.

00:44:23.657 --> 00:44:24.923
I didn't blink.

00:44:25.597 --> 00:44:28.385
And neither would you. So
you knew all along, then.

00:44:28.389 --> 00:44:31.102
You knew the vampires
weren't killing anyone.

00:44:31.318 --> 00:44:32.912
You knew about the cattle,

00:44:32.916 --> 00:44:35.344
And you just didn't
care. Care about what?

00:44:35.449 --> 00:44:38.105
A nest of vampires suddenly acting nice,

00:44:38.108 --> 00:44:40.782
Taking a little time out
from sucking innocent people,

00:44:40.789 --> 00:44:42.325
And we're supposed to buy that?

00:44:42.449 --> 00:44:43.364
Trust me.

00:44:44.939 --> 00:44:46.545
It doesn't change what they are.

00:44:48.376 --> 00:44:49.633
And I can prove it.

00:44:53.907 --> 00:44:54.814
Let him go.

00:44:57.619 --> 00:44:58.472
Now!

00:44:58.557 --> 00:45:01.733
Relax. If I wanted to kill
him, he'd be on the floor.

00:45:02.597 --> 00:45:03.943
Just making a little point.

00:45:19.818 --> 00:45:21.304
Think she's so different?

00:45:23.856 --> 00:45:25.764
Still want to save her? Look at her.

00:45:30.079 --> 00:45:31.304
They're all the same.

00:45:31.970 --> 00:45:32.852
Evil,

00:45:32.949 --> 00:45:34.222
Bloodthirsty.

00:45:39.956 --> 00:45:40.913
No.

00:45:41.500 --> 00:45:42.461
No.

00:45:44.737 --> 00:45:46.414
You hear her, Gordon?

00:45:46.907 --> 00:45:47.922
No.

00:45:55.177 --> 00:45:56.583
We're done here.

00:45:58.177 --> 00:46:00.164
Sam, get her out of here. Yeah.

00:46:06.978 --> 00:46:07.853
Gordon,

00:46:09.659 --> 00:46:11.815
I think you and I got
some things to talk about.

00:46:25.719 --> 00:46:26.813
Get out of my way.

00:46:27.927 --> 00:46:28.702
Sorry.

00:46:28.809 --> 00:46:29.934
You're not serious.

00:46:33.289 --> 00:46:35.813
I'm having a hard time believing
it, too, but I know what I saw.

00:46:35.818 --> 00:46:37.865
If you want those vampires,
you got to go through me.

00:46:46.259 --> 00:46:47.063
Fine.

00:47:08.197 --> 00:47:11.044
What are you doing, man?
You doing this for a fang?

00:47:12.028 --> 00:47:14.251
Come on, Dean, we're
on the same side here.

00:47:14.257 --> 00:47:16.195
I don't think so, you sadistic bastard.

00:47:21.659 --> 00:47:23.382
You're not like your brother.

00:47:23.479 --> 00:47:24.514
You're a killer

00:47:24.759 --> 00:47:25.695
Like me.

00:47:51.369 --> 00:47:52.664
Oh, sorry.

00:47:55.410 --> 00:47:56.452
You know,

00:47:57.358 --> 00:47:58.773
I might be like you.

00:47:59.829 --> 00:48:00.942
I might not.

00:48:07.169 --> 00:48:09.162
But you're the one tied up right now.

00:48:50.280 --> 00:48:51.403
I miss anything?

00:48:52.669 --> 00:48:53.454
Eh, not much.

00:48:55.267 --> 00:48:56.483
Lenore get out okay?

00:48:56.749 --> 00:48:57.445
Yeah,

00:48:57.948 --> 00:48:59.233
All of them did.

00:49:02.669 --> 00:49:04.373
Then, I guess our work here is done.

00:49:07.259 --> 00:49:08.262
How are you doing, Gordie?

00:49:09.657 --> 00:49:10.692
Got to tinkle yet?

00:49:11.557 --> 00:49:12.414
All right.

00:49:13.597 --> 00:49:14.831
Well, get comfy.

00:49:15.447 --> 00:49:18.961
We'll call someone in two or
three days, have them come out

00:49:18.970 --> 00:49:19.985
And untie you.

00:49:21.999 --> 00:49:23.331
Ready to go, Dean?

00:49:24.930 --> 00:49:25.831
Not yet.

00:49:32.410 --> 00:49:33.954
I guess this is goodbye.

00:49:35.458 --> 00:49:36.492
Well, it's...

00:49:36.950 --> 00:49:37.954
It's been real.

00:49:48.927 --> 00:49:49.942
Okay.

00:49:50.447 --> 00:49:51.452
I'm good now.

00:49:52.767 --> 00:49:53.583
We can go.

00:50:07.677 --> 00:50:09.483
Sam. Yeah?

00:50:10.538 --> 00:50:11.425
Clock me one.

00:50:13.007 --> 00:50:14.103
What? Come on.

00:50:14.217 --> 00:50:15.423
I won't even hit you back.

00:50:15.559 --> 00:50:16.372
Let's go.

00:50:18.706 --> 00:50:19.423
No.

00:50:20.077 --> 00:50:22.323
Let's go. You get a
freebie. Hit me. Come on.

00:50:23.018 --> 00:50:25.711
You look like you just went 12
rounds with a block of cement, Dean.

00:50:26.807 --> 00:50:27.905
I'll take a rain check.

00:50:31.717 --> 00:50:33.172
I wish we never took this job.

00:50:33.186 --> 00:50:34.313
It just jacked everything up.

00:50:36.249 --> 00:50:37.072
What do you mean?

00:50:40.588 --> 00:50:43.262
Think about all the hunts we
went on, Sammy, our whole lives.

00:50:44.048 --> 00:50:45.954
What if we killed things
that didn't deserve killing?

00:50:46.487 --> 00:50:48.543
You know? I mean, the way dad raised us.

00:50:48.809 --> 00:50:50.573
Dean, after what happened to mom...

00:50:52.407 --> 00:50:55.173
Dad did the best he
could. I know he did.

00:50:56.668 --> 00:50:58.115
But maybe he wasn't perfect.

00:50:58.708 --> 00:51:00.902
And the way he raised us,
to hate those things...

00:51:00.909 --> 00:51:02.032
And, man, I hate them.

00:51:02.157 --> 00:51:03.463
I do.

00:51:03.680 --> 00:51:05.943
When I killed that vampire at the
mill, I didn't even think about it.

00:51:05.960 --> 00:51:07.385
Hell, I even enjoyed it.

00:51:10.537 --> 00:51:11.873
You didn't kill Lenore.

00:51:12.509 --> 00:51:14.162
No, but every instinct told me to.

00:51:14.568 --> 00:51:16.282
I was gonna kill her. I
was gonna kill them all.

00:51:16.289 --> 00:51:17.573
Yeah, Dean, but you didn't,

00:51:18.037 --> 00:51:19.372
And that's what matters.

00:51:23.338 --> 00:51:24.544
Yeah.

00:51:28.169 --> 00:51:29.793
'Cause you're a pain in my ass.

00:51:32.930 --> 00:51:35.382
I guess I might have to stick
around to be a pain in the ass, then.

00:51:36.769 --> 00:51:37.561
Thanks.

00:51:40.650 --> 00:51:41.623
Don't mention it.



